zefciu wrote:
> Ok, there are many many spin-offs of NH.  (NH is after all a spin-off of
> Rogue).  But they all cover the same old quest-for-AoY story.  But did
> anyone think about the sequel of Nethack?  Ok, the player got that
> demigodhoodness, the god his "deserved ascendance", but what happened then?

As everyone else has noted, the player's character is a demigod at the
end of the game, so there's not really a lot of places it could go.  If
there were, then the game probably shouldn't have ended just yet.

But think for a moment: why do other computer game get lots of sequels?
 It generally isn't because there is another story that desperately
needs telling, but that the company that publishes it wants to acquire
another pile of money, to put alongside the one gained from the first
game.  They seek to "establish a franchise" or some such rubbish, while
no one makes any money off of Nethack.  That's just one way the
commercial development system does computer games a disservice; there
are plenty of others.

But anyway, no one plays Nethack for the story, or at least not for the
one hard-coded into the game.

